From ff58016c1be5bde17adcd2663cd627e54e5c7063 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mahesh Vaidya <mahesh.vaidya@altera.com>
Date: Sun, 24 May 2026 11:54:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: phy_caps: Advertise sub-2500 speeds for 2500BASE-X

Add CONFIG_PHY_CAPS_MRPHY_DR_2500BASEX. When set,
phy_caps_from_interface() returns 10M / 100M / 1G in addition to
2500FD for the 2500BASE-X interface mode.

This supports hardware that can dynamically reconfigure the
2500BASE-X serdes between 1G and 2.5G profiles (Altera Agilex 5
Multirate PHY with DR controller). Gated by Kconfig so that
non-MRPHY drivers, which cannot run a 2500BASE-X SerDes at sub-2500
rates, are unaffected.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Mahesh Vaidya <mahesh.vaidya@altera.com>
---
 drivers/net/phy/Kconfig    |  9 +++++++++
 drivers/net/phy/phy_caps.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig b/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig
index 98700d069191..d3ad5107df08 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/Kconfig
@@ -76,6 +76,15 @@ config RUST_PHYLIB_ABSTRACTIONS
           Adds support needed for PHY drivers written in Rust. It provides
           a wrapper around the C phylib core.
 
+config PHY_CAPS_MRPHY_DR_2500BASEX
+	bool "Advertise sub-2500 speeds for 2500BASE-X (Altera MRPHY DR)"
+	help
+	  When set, phy_caps_from_interface() returns the sub-2500 link
+	  capabilities (10M, 100M, 1G) in addition to 2500FD for the
+	  2500BASE-X interface mode, supporting hardware that can
+	  dynamically reconfigure the 2500BASE-X serdes (e.g., the
+	  Altera Agilex 5 Multirate PHY).
+
 config SFP
 	tristate "SFP cage support"
 	depends on I2C && PHYLINK
diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/phy_caps.c b/drivers/net/phy/phy_caps.c
index 23c808b59b6f..171128de3e58 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/phy_caps.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phy_caps.c
@@ -333,6 +333,19 @@ unsigned long phy_caps_from_interface(phy_interface_t interface)
 
 	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_2500BASEX:
 		link_caps |= BIT(LINK_CAPA_2500FD);
+#ifdef CONFIG_PHY_CAPS_MRPHY_DR_2500BASEX
+		/*
+		 * Altera Agilex 5 Multirate PHY with Dynamic
+		 * Reconfiguration: a 2500BASE-X interface can switch
+		 * the XCVR to a 1G profile at runtime, supporting
+		 * 10M / 100M / 1G via MRPHY sub-rate adaptation.
+		 * Advertise these so PHY-side autoneg can settle on a
+		 * sub-2500 speed when the link partner is not 2.5G capable.
+		 */
+		link_caps |= BIT(LINK_CAPA_1000HD) | BIT(LINK_CAPA_1000FD);
+		link_caps |= BIT(LINK_CAPA_100HD)  | BIT(LINK_CAPA_100FD);
+		link_caps |= BIT(LINK_CAPA_10HD)   | BIT(LINK_CAPA_10FD);
+#endif
 		break;
 
 	case PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_5GBASER:
-- 
